  "body": "Writer record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4262#issuecomment-7209042252\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/midpose.rs`: the swing bound counts the B letter at `max |cos A|` over the move. A and C keep full weight. A new helper `max_abs_cos` gives the weight. A non-finite letter gives weight 1, which is the old bound.\n- The module header states the new proof.\n- One pinning test in `posed_steel_tests.rs` and one soundness test in `midpose.rs`.\n- `docs/decisions/4262-housing-table-index.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe mid-pose walk bounds the axis turn in an interval from the letters' sweep. It counted each letter at one radian for each radian. The axis is `Rz(C) (cos A sin B, -sin A, cos A cos B)`, so B turns it only `|cos A|` for each radian.\n\n`axis_to_angles` writes a radial pose under the A line as B180 and the same pose over it as B0. At A = -90 the pose crosses the equator with a B 180 -> 0 flip and no real turn. The old bound read that flip as a swing of about 90 degrees on one interval. The posed fixture sweep then grew the spindle housing capsule (300+ mm up the pose) by hundreds of mm. The grown capsule reached the machine table 510 mm below the axis. The post refused with \"spindle housing at move N strikes a fixture\".\n\nThis answers the question of the issue: the frames are correct. The refusal was phantom. It came from the swing bound, not from the frame math. The same bound inflated the part-frame fallback too.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `verify::posed_steel::tests::a_b_flip_at_the_pole_of_a_turning_a_does_not_swing_the_housing_into_the_table` (camcraft-sim lib). A tip 10 mm off the A line, the pose flips B180 -> B0 at A -90, the Doosan housing (r 75, 250 long), the Doosan table (top Z-510). It asserts Clear in the machine frame and no hit in the part frame, for +Y and -Y.\n  - Red before the fix: `left: Hit(Spindle) right: Clear` (\"machine frame, pose [0.0, 1.0, 1e-9]\").\n- Soundness: `verify::midpose::tests::the_cos_a_weighted_bound_holds_near_the_pole`. Four letter pairs near the pole, 64 samples in each interval: no pose inside an interval strays past its swing. A B flip at the pole gives a swing under 1e-8.\n- Mutation 1: the old rate line back -> both tests red. Fix back -> both green.\n- Mutation 2: `max_abs_cos` forced to 0 (an under-report) -> the soundness tests stay green. On the canonical letters the end-pose angles of each interval already bound the interior, so the letter-rate term rarely decides. The weight is proven from the derivative norms (decision file), not from this test.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head a5b1958eb: 135 steps, 0 failed. The base moved during the run, so the plan was wider than the diff. It includes `app suites: example_catalog` (44 passed, 4 ignored).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy`: not run. This is a P3 PR. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a P3 PR no heavy step. The dry-run reach is 115 release steps. They run at the cut.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suite ran green and no `*.nc` or `*.cl` file changed. The change only makes a proven bound tighter, so a verdict can only go from hit to clear.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The reporter's project file. It is not in the issue. A model built from the issue text (R 9 x 30 cylinder on X, 30 x 44 x 44 box stock, 3 mm ball, Doosan + table, nose_to_axis stated) gave no fixture strike on main. It was refused for other reasons (uncut stock, a B word). So the end-to-end post of the report is not pinned. The pin reproduces the reported verdict at the sim law.\n- The UI playback display (finding 1 of the contributor comment). It is display only and not part of this fix.\n- The message does not name the struck box yet. That changes the `FixtureHit` warning and its readers. A follow-up issue will track it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `verify/midpose.rs` or `verify/posed_steel*.rs`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The post no longer refuses a Rotary Flow on a turning A with a phantom \"spindle housing strikes a fixture\" when the radial pose crosses the A line's equator.\n\nFixes #4262\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
